    {q:'Which of these keeps its own shape?', o:['A solid, like a pebble','A liquid, like orange juice','A gas, like the air in a balloon'], a:0, type:'Find it', why:'Solids keep their shape. Liquids flow and gases spread out.'},
    {q:'What does evaporation mean?', o:['When a liquid turns into a gas','When a gas turns into a liquid','When a liquid turns into a solid'], a:0, type:'Word power', why:'The puddle evaporated: liquid water turned into invisible water vapour.'},
    {q:'What does condensation mean?', o:['When a gas cools and turns back into a liquid','When ice melts','When water boils'], a:0, type:'Word power', why:'Water vapour condensed on the cold mirror and the cold can.'},
    {q:'Why did the water in the cupboard saucer hardly change?', o:['It was cool and there was no wind','The cupboard was too small','Biscuit drank it'], a:0, type:'Think about it', why:'Evaporation is slowest where it is cool and the air is still.'},
    {q:'Why was the water in the cup not salty?', o:['The salt was left behind when the water evaporated','Felix added sugar','The cling film soaked up the salt'], a:0, type:'Think about it', why:'Only the water evaporates. The salt stays in the bowl.'},
    {q:'Which mystery came straight after the melting chocolate?', o:['Making ice lollies and measuring melting ice','The misty bathroom mirror','The paddling pool'], a:0, type:'Order it', why:'Puddle, chocolate, ice and lollies, boiling water, saucers, mirror, greenhouse, bowl, then the paddling pool.'}
